# Settings from a MIDI controller (0.16.18): a map learned on the editor page (setmap.bin, made by web/fm1backup.js mmEncode: CC 13 on channel 1
# a fader on the acid's Cutoff, CC 14 an encoder (64 +- n) on the Tempo, CC 15 a fader on the Mode (the scale), CC 16 an encoder (1 up, 127 down)
# on the pad's level, and a pad note 36 on channel 10 as PLAY, the panel's own as before). A map with settings is MAP2. A learned CC sets its
# setting straight, on any page: lit on the page that shows it, its name and value a moment elsewhere.
seed 0
loadobj 24 tests/scenarios/setmap.bin
restore 24
expect rsvalid 1
reboot
wait 3000
expect playing 1
expect view 0
# the fader on the acid's Cutoff (0 .. 100) from the Tempo page: the ends and the middle; not on this page, so a message
midi B0 0D 7F
wait 100
expect par34 100
expect msgon 1
expect touched -1
midi B0 0D 00
wait 100
expect par34 0
midi B0 0D 40
wait 100
expect par34 50
# another channel: not this map's
midi B1 0D 7F
wait 100
expect par34 50
# the encoder on the Tempo (70 .. 190): steps, and on this page its knob is lit
setpar 5 120
wait 100
midi B0 0E 45
wait 100
expect par5 125
expect touched 0
midi B0 0E 3D
wait 100
expect par5 122
# the Mode, as the ALGORITHM dial sets it: the scale's notes too (0 Ionian)
midi B0 0F 00
wait 100
expect par72 0
expect pool 0xAB5
# the pad's level, 1 up / 127 down, from the FX menu
setpar 0 50
tap FX
wait 300
midi B0 10 03
wait 100
expect par0 53
midi B0 10 7E
wait 100
expect par0 51
midi B0 0D 7F
wait 100
expect par34 100
tap FX
wait 300
# the panel's own entries still work beside the settings: the pad as PLAY
midi 99 24 7F
wait 60
midi 89 24 00
wait 200
expect playing 0
# a damaged map is refused whole
restore 24 bad
expect rsvalid 0
